# Core contribution standards

- Follow patterns in the surrounding code.
- Keep changes focused and avoid over-engineering.
- Add tests for new functionality.
- Prevent XSS, SQL injection, and command injection at trust boundaries.
- Keep frontend and backend work in separate PRs when practical because they deploy at different cadences.

## Comments

- Comment only to explain why, an invariant, or non-obvious logic needed to change code safely.
- Do not narrate self-explanatory code.
- Never put Slack, GitHub, Jira, or other links in code comments.

## Human review gate

Before `git push`, summarize the changes and obtain explicit human approval. A request to open a PR expresses intent but does not itself authorize pushing.
